From 1448c0fd0d055206735da290480ac8f7adefbe6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:33:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gweb: Fix crash on malformed http response

A response whose first header line starts with a space or tab was
handled as a continuation line before any header had been seen, and
handle_multi_line() looked up a NULL last_key, which crashes in
g_str_hash(). One malformed reply from the MMSC stops mmsd.

Backported from ConnMan commit 22901212105055 ("gweb: Fix crash on
malformed http response") by Mans Rullgard <mans@mansr.com>. Upstream
message:

  If an http response has a line starting with whitespace before the
  first valid header field, g_hash_table_lookup() is called with a NULL
  key, which is invalid.  Fix this by checking for a valid last_key
  before attempting to process continuation lines.

  Based on a patch by Tomasz Bursztyka for an issue originally reported
  by Marcel Mulder.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Backport [https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/network/connman/connman.git/commit/?id=22901212105055b24f73504a74f5a57eee809777]
---
 gweb/gweb.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gweb/gweb.c b/gweb/gweb.c
index d434b1b..327f48b 100644
--- a/gweb/gweb.c
+++ b/gweb/gweb.c
@@ -779,6 +779,9 @@ static void handle_multi_line(struct web_session *session)
 	char *str;
 	gchar *value;
 
+	if (!session->result.last_key)
+		return;
+
 	str = session->current_header->str;
 
 	if (str[0] != ' ' && str[0] != '\t')
-- 
